  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "New: ReadGrouped<TParent, TChild, TKey>() for one-to-many joins; WithTransaction() / WithoutTransaction().\n\nBEHAVIOUR CHANGE (PostgreSQL): a run no longer opens an explicit transaction by default. PostgreSQL already executes a batch as one implicit transaction, so BEGIN/COMMIT added two round-trips and no atomicity. Batches remain all-or-nothing; reads are ~45% faster. SQL Server and SQLite are unchanged.\n\nBREAKING (PostgreSQL): setting an isolation level now throws unless you also call WithTransaction(), because a level cannot be applied to a run that opens no transaction. One-line fix; the exception says so.\n\nFull notes: https://github.com/purelogictek-inc/DapperPipeline/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
